# Accepted risks for the container scan — TEMPORARY, reviewed on every change.
# Remove an entry as soon as a fixed upstream release ships.
#
# All findings are pip's OWN vendored copies, not application dependencies.
# pip 26.2 (2026-07-29) began shipping a CycloneDX SBOM of its vendored
# libraries (pip/_vendor/bom.cdx.json); trivy ingests in-image SBOMs, so these
# internal copies became visible to the scan even though nothing in this
# project installs or imports them. A bare `python:3.12-slim` image with only
# `pip install --upgrade pip` reproduced exactly the msgpack and setuptools
# findings when they first appeared (2026-08-03).

# msgpack vendored inside pip (pip/_vendor/msgpack), used only by pip's own HTTP
# cache; the Unpacker-reuse out-of-bounds read requires feeding it
# attacker-controlled msgpack streams, which never happens in this image.
GHSA-6v7p-g79w-8964

# setuptools: pip vendors only the pkg_resources subpackage — the vulnerable
# PackageIndex/easy_install code path is not shipped in the image.
CVE-2025-47273

# urllib3 2.7.0 vendored inside pip (pip/_vendor/urllib3), fixed in 2.8.0.
# Flagged from 2026-10-05; pip 26.2.1, the newest pip, still pins 2.7.0 in
# pip/_vendor/vendor.txt. Only pip imports this copy, and pip runs only while
# the image is built: the image itself runs pytest.
#
# GHSA-8988-9cw3-xx77: the target server's TLS settings can override an HTTPS
# proxy's. It matters only when pip goes through an HTTPS proxy; the CI build
# uses none.
CVE-2026-97687

# GHSA-vxq7-64xx-v4gw: a malicious server streaming a chunked response can make
# urllib3 buffer an unbounded chunk-size line. The build downloads only from
# PyPI over TLS, so the worst case is memory exhaustion during the build.
CVE-2026-97689
